  "notes": "Found by a search over the cyclic group Z_81 on 2026-11-21. The skew first block and the 3-compressions of the other three blocks (a solution of the compressed problem over Z_27) are fixed in advance; every lift of each compressed block is enumerated, the lifts whose periodic autocorrelations lie in five-value windows form three pools, and the pools are joined exactly. The join stopped at its first solution, so this is a sample and not a census. A skew-Hadamard matrix of order 324 has been known since 1994, from supplementary difference sets in the elementary abelian group of order 81 (second source); the order is not new and is not among the open orders of baselines/skew-gaps.json. What this entry supplies is a quadruple with a skew block over the cyclic group Z_81. A search of current sources on 2026-11-21 found no earlier one; that is a report of the search, not a proof of priority. This is the board's first quadruple with a skew block at n=81."
